sequenceDiagram
    participant U as Client
    participant B as Booking service
    participant I as Inventory DB
    participant D as Bookings DB
    participant P as Payment service
    U->>B: POST /v1/bookings with Idempotency-Key
    B->>D: insert idempotency row, fails if key exists then return stored result
    B->>I: BEGIN, UPDATE room_inventory SET reserved = reserved + 1 WHERE hotel, room type, date IN nights AND reserved + 1 <= total + allowance
    I-->>B: affected rows
    alt affected rows equals number of nights
        B->>D: insert reservation PENDING with expires_at = now + 10 min, same transaction as outbox row
        B->>I: COMMIT
        B-->>U: 201 PENDING with reservation_id
        U->>B: POST /v1/bookings/id/pay with payment token
        B->>P: authorize and capture with idempotency key = reservation_id
        P-->>B: captured
        B->>D: reservation CONFIRMED plus outbox BookingConfirmed
        B-->>U: 200 CONFIRMED
    else fewer rows updated
        B->>I: ROLLBACK
        B-->>U: 409 sold out for those nights
    end
    Note over B,I: Sweeper later turns expired PENDING holds into EXPIRED and decrements reserved for each night.
